<<~ ahu #/head>>

! What a Nexus Wants Members FOR ~ open, and it gates the rest

> ''PLACEHOLDER.'' A question with a shaped rim and no answer. Minted so the talk-story that answers it has somewhere to pour.

''The finding that raises it.'' Surveying admission across institutions: where admitting a newcomer ''required expropriating a named incumbent'' — guild mastership, chattel status, a sponsor's claim — routine peacetime machinery essentially does not appear. Where ''no incumbent claim existed'' — auxiliary service, statutory naturalisation — standing peacetime machinery ran for centuries. ''Emergency lowers a third party's price for overriding a claim; it never creates the appetite.''

So the operative variable reads: ''does the collective want something the incumbent cannot veto?'' Rome wanted soldiers and ran diplomas for centuries. Venice wanted taxpayers and the Senate granted without asking the merchants. ''This stack has never answered it for itself.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/why-it-gates>>

!! Why it gates

The conversion act (`the-thing-event`) runs on an assembly standing as the third party — the host presents, the realm receives, and the host is paid in depth for the gift rather than in a dependant kept. ''That inversion needs the layer to WANT the newcomer.'' Absent an appetite of its own, the assembly has nothing to pay with and the shape collapses back to the dyad.

''And a second consequence rides here'': a process reading entails that composition runs BOTH ways — an entity at N+1 must supply enabling conditions for its members' standing at N, ''by acting rather than by registering''. What a Nexus wants members for and what a Nexus does for its members read as one question from two ends.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/open>>

!! To pour here later

* What does a Nexus produce, hold, or carry that more dwellers make ''better'' rather than merely ''larger''?
* Does the answer differ per realm — and if each realm answers it alone, does the mesh need any answer at all?
* ''The Gilbert tension'', unresolved and adjacent: a joint commitment //rescindable only jointly// persists as a standing normative state ''precisely because it is not activity'' — and a layer deposits ''by'' activity. This stack carries both.

<<~/ahu>>

